{"id": "1530568662606544918", "channel_id": "1515634790076907610", "author_id": "420344732409921536", "author_name": "diluteworm19816", "content": "Honestly, turning Arcane Dominion into a daily activity could work. Now, the people who argued that it would harm the developers' income due to paid packs becoming obsolete are correct. Morimens is already very f2p friendly in my opinion, so there's really no need to push for changes that would screw the devs and us in the long run. \nSo, here's what I cooked up while making lunch: \nPlayers can run arcane dominion once a day. The first time you do so per week has guaranteed drops of each rarity (number varies, but we get the green, blue, and purple mats). The following times, there is *a chance* of getting more mats (maybe guaranteed green ones, the rest up to rng). \nThere could even be a repeatable (daily) new level that has all materials in a random pool of rewards, or alternatively, a new level that has two to three types of materials in its reward pool and changes every week.  Like, week 1 is the faces and the cord thing, then week 2 it's butterfly wings and *insert material here, I forgot which ones exist*. \nLike this, there's a new daily activity to pad out the game without completely ruining the material economy. Paid packs are still relevant for whales but f2p players will get more mats to enhance their favorite teams.", "timestamp": "2026-07-25T13:33:25.756000+00:00", "thread_id": "1515634790076907610", "reactions": [{"emoji": "👍", "emoji_id": null, "count": 1}]}
